  "question": {
    "text": "If the integral <math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8747;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> (where,&nbsp;<math><mi>C</mi></math> is the constant of integration), then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>K</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
